(7248887, 1125709, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pearlseyes:</b></div><hr/><i> Wth?  Some times I don''t understand the voters.  Has your camera been altered for Ir photography or is it just sensitive? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m glad you like the photo - and I''ve given up trying to understand the voters.  Yes, this is taken with an IR converted Nikon D7000 using a Sigma 8-16mm zoom.  The shutter was engaged with the zoom at 16mm and I zoomed out during the exposure period doing my best to keep the sun spot steady.  Handheld shot at 1/30, so it''s a fast zoom and not quite as hard as it sounds.<br/> <br/>Again, thanks for the comment, and I''m glad you like it.</td>', 'Originally posted by pearlseyes: Wth?  Some times I don''t understand the voters.  Has your camera been altered for Ir photography or is it just sensitive?   I''m glad you like the photo - and I''ve given up trying to understand the voters.  Yes, this is taken with an IR converted Nikon D7000 using a Sigma 8-16mm zoom.  The shutter was engaged with the zoom at 16mm and I zoomed out during the exposure period doing my best to keep the sun spot steady.  Handheld shot at 1/30, so it''s a fast zoom and not quite as hard as it sounds. Again, thanks for the comment, and I''m glad you like it.', '2014-08-08 06:23:15.000000', NULL, 0),
